- Static Arrays:
    {
        uint16[13];
    }
- Dynamic arrays:
    {
        uint8 count;
        uint16[count]; // If in same packet
        // OR
        uint16[PacketName.count]; // If in other packet
    }
- Complex Enums:
    {
        enum uint8 EVENTS {
            E_ONE = 1 { detailSize: 2 },
            E_TWO { detailSize: 1 },
            E_THREE { detailSize: 0 }
        }

        EVENTS event;
        byte details[event.detailSize];
    }
- Repeat fields:
    {
        repeat (10) {
            byte eventHeader
            uint payload
        }

        uint counter
        repeat (counter) { ... }
    }
- Complex Conditional checking in branches:
    branch {
        SEGMENT1 if (currentByte < 0xA3);
        SEGMENT2 if (cyrrentByte >= VAR_DEF); // Include operations like + - * / %?
    }
    
- Mathematical expressions in values:
    {
        uint16 val {
            expr: bytes * 2
        }
    }
- Binary operators in values? -> May not be needed simply because of the nature of bitfields
- STD math functions
- Loops/repeats
- In file byte processing:
    {
        interpret 656ED7 as PacketName
        ("004FE3", "PacketName")
    }
- File output assigning:
    {
        dump PacketName1, PacketName2 as "JSON" // OR

        dump * as "JSON" { // Each packet gets its own file with the file name being the timestamp
            includeTimestamp: true,
            includeTawBytes: true,
            includePacketName: true,
            destinationFolder: "./folder/path"
        }
    }
- STD Mynic files for popular protocols, such as the TCP network protocol
- Date/Time/Seconds STD datatypes
- bitsX datatype, similar to uint, X can be any positive int